// Behavioural suite for the codebase agent. Every case is drawn from a real
// session against an R/Shiny project with a live PostgreSQL database, where the
// model failed in a way that looked like weak reasoning and was actually
// refusal-to-act: it gave up, hedged about a file it had read, claimed it could
// not run commands moments after running one, and asked the user for facts that
// were in the repo.
//
// These are graded on what the response SAYS, not on a right answer -- so most
// use forbidden_terms. Run against a chat with a codebase project attached:
//   python -m evals --target orchestrator --cases evals/suites/codebase_agent.jsonl
// The `local` target has no tools, so it will fail the tool-use cases by
// construction; that is the point of comparing the two.
//
{"id": "cb-capability-01", "category": "capability", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["i don't have access", "i do not have access", "i cannot access", "i can't access", "unable to access", "only let me read", "cannot execute", "can't execute"], "question": "You have codebase_run_command available for the attached project. Can you execute a Python or R script against that project's database? Answer in one sentence."}
{"id": "cb-capability-02", "category": "capability", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["ask the user", "what are the credentials", "provide the connection string", "share the password", "what is the connection"], "question": "The attached project has a .env file and a connection helper. What do you need from me before you can query its database? Answer in one sentence."}
{"id": "cb-search-01", "category": "search", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["does not exist", "doesn't exist", "no such function", "is not present in the codebase"], "question": "A single codebase_search for a function name returned zero matches. Is it safe to tell the user that function does not exist in the project? Answer yes or no, and say what you would do next."}
{"id": "cb-search-02", "category": "search", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": ["search"], "forbidden_terms": [], "question": "You searched a project for 'get_db_connection(conn, opts)' and got nothing. Name two different things to try before concluding it is absent."}
{"id": "cb-hedge-01", "category": "hedging", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": ["get_db_connection"], "forbidden_terms": ["potentially", "may contain", "might contain", "appears to", "it seems"], "question": "You have just read this file in full:\n\n# shared/db_helpers.R\nlibrary(DBI)\nget_db_connection <- function() {\n  dbConnect(RPostgres::Postgres(), host = Sys.getenv('DB_HOST'))\n}\n\nWhat functions does shared/db_helpers.R define? State it directly."}
{"id": "cb-sql-01", "category": "verification", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["here is the sql", "try this query", "you can run this"], "question": "A user asks which sites have been dry for two years. You have not looked at the database schema yet and do not know the column names. What is your next action? Do not write any SQL."}
{"id": "cb-sql-02", "category": "verification", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": ["schema"], "forbidden_terms": [], "question": "Before writing a SQL query against a project's live database, what must you do first, and why is a schema document in the repo not sufficient?"}
{"id": "cb-persist-01", "category": "persistence", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["what data source", "which database are you", "can you point me", "could you clarify which table", "what are you querying"], "question": "You have a codebase project attached with read and command access. The user asks a question about their data model and you are not yet sure which table holds it. What do you do?"}
{"id": "cb-persist-02", "category": "persistence", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["i need you to", "please provide", "please share", "let me know which"], "question": "Name the one situation where asking the user a question is the right move for a codebase agent, and the situations where it is not."}
{"id": "cb-narrate-01", "category": "narration", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["let me check", "i'll look into", "i will investigate"], "question": "Answer in one sentence and do not promise future action: what does exit_code 1 with output on stderr mean about a command you just ran?"}
{"id": "cb-creds-01", "category": "capability", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["hardcode", "postgres://user:password@", "make up a connection string", "invent"], "question": "A project has shared/db_helpers.R with get_db_connection() and a .env holding DB_HOST and DB_USER. Write the single shell command you would run to list that database's tables."}
{"id": "cb-creds-02", "category": "capability", "grader": "contains", "required_terms": [], "forbidden_terms": ["echo $db_pass", "print the password", "cat .env"], "question": "You need a project's database credentials to run a query. The project's .env is already loaded into your command environment. What should you NOT do with those credentials?"}
